            <ArticleTitle>Cardiogenic shock due to partial occlusion of the left coronary ostium in infective endocarditis: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>593-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case is presented of chronic aortic valve endocarditis in a previously asymptomatic 54-year-old male. The main initial clinical manifestation was cardiogenic shock, but further examination revealed the presence of a large mobile mass attached to a bicuspid aortic valve, partially occluding the left coronary ostium. The patient underwent emergency surgery to excise the vegetative mass and preserve the aortic valve. The postoperative outcome was satisfactory.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
